<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44158" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκαιρ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well-timed,
			seasonable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philem.
					113
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
					116
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδατα</span> (rainfall) <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				8.7.6
			</span></i>; <i>nihil</i> -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότερον</span>
			<i>epistula tua</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				4.7.1
			</span></i>: c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χὥ τι σοι λέγειν εὔκαιρόν ἐστι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Nat.</u>
				28.4
			</span></i>; -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότερον ἔσται διελθεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					12.9.7
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὔκαιρον,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐκαιρία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Din.</u>
				7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μέτριον καὶ τὸ εὔ. ἐν ἡδοναῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristo Stoic.
					1.86
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκαιρον ἀείσας</span>
			<i>in season</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				5.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of places,
				<i>convenient, well situated</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόποι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PPetr.</u>
					2p.28
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>, 
				Sup.
			), cf.<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				4.38.1
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			), <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.63
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>rich, wealthy</i>, dub.l. in St. Byz.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χαττηνία</span>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ρως</span>
			<i>seasonably, opportunely</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Medic.</u>
				3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nico
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				38.28
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, al., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. χρῆσθαί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					5.143
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ἔχειν πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					11.12
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				582a28
			</span></i>; <i>favourably, propitiously,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PCair.Zen.
				46
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				2086r
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				6
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐκερως</span> Pap.): 
				Comp.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότερον</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				78a
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότατα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				5.63.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ-ρως ἔχειν</span> to have no
				<i>leisure</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.26.10
			</span></i>.</div>
